Venetium 0044 - ARM32 sandboxed utility processes run at USER_LIMITED, not USER_LOCKDOWN (fixes 'cannot unzip crx').
The utility analogue of 0043: on Win10 ARM32/15035 a child created with the USER_LOCKDOWN primary token dies because the
parallel loader's worker threads open DLLs under the primary token, not the main-thread impersonation. The CRX unpacker's
data_decoder/unzip utilities (kService/kUtility) still got USER_LOCKDOWN. Before PreSpawnChild, under ARCH_CPU_ARMEL,
raise any utility whose lockdown token is USER_LOCKDOWN to USER_LIMITED (catches the generic lockdown types + IconReader/
ScreenAI; leaves network/audio/CDM/proxy and the already-USER_LIMITED types untouched). Still a real restricted-token
sandbox. x86 keeps USER_LOCKDOWN.

diff --git a/content/browser/service_host/utility_sandbox_delegate_win.cc b/content/browser/service_host/utility_sandbox_delegate_win.cc
--- a/content/browser/service_host/utility_sandbox_delegate_win.cc
+++ b/content/browser/service_host/utility_sandbox_delegate_win.cc
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 #include "base/synchronization/waitable_event.h"
 #include "base/win/scoped_handle.h"
 #include "base/win/windows_handle_util.h"
+#include "build/build_config.h"
 #include "content/public/browser/content_browser_client.h"
 #include "content/public/browser/sandboxed_process_launcher_delegate.h"
 #include "content/public/common/content_client.h"
@@ -440,6 +441,27 @@
     }
   }
 
+#if defined(ARCH_CPU_ARMEL)
+  // Venetium 0044: Windows 10 ARM32 (Tegra, build 15035) maps a process's DLLs on parallel
+  // loader worker threads that run under the process PRIMARY token. A sandboxed utility created
+  // with the USER_LOCKDOWN primary token (its only restricting SID is the NULL SID) therefore
+  // cannot open its DLLs and dies before it runs -- the same mechanism Venetium 0043 fixed for
+  // the renderer, one process type over. It surfaced as "cannot unzip crx": the Web Store CRX
+  // unpacker's data_decoder / unzip utilities (kService / kUtility) run at USER_LOCKDOWN. Raise
+  // any lockdown utility to USER_LIMITED -- the token the GPU process already runs with on this
+  // hardware -- so the loader worker threads can read the DLLs, while keeping a real
+  // restricted-token sandbox. Looser types (network/audio/CDM/proxy at USER_UNPROTECTED, and the
+  // speech/model/print utilities already at USER_LIMITED) are not USER_LOCKDOWN and stay as they
+  // are. x86 keeps USER_LOCKDOWN (this is guarded to ARM32).
+  if (config->GetLockdownTokenLevel() == sandbox::USER_LOCKDOWN) {
+    auto result = config->SetTokenLevel(sandbox::USER_RESTRICTED_SAME_ACCESS,
+                                        sandbox::USER_LIMITED);
+    if (result != sandbox::SBOX_ALL_OK) {
+      return false;
+    }
+  }
+#endif  // defined(ARCH_CPU_ARMEL)
+
   return GetContentClient()->browser()->PreSpawnChild(
       config, sandbox_type_,
       ContentBrowserClient::ChildSpawnFlags::kChildSpawnFlagNone);
